[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689245618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2689245618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2689245618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gSqGy","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T22:26:35Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T22:27:34Z","body":"@MichaelDawe Mouse capture is supported on Android and is being used in the Godot Android editor (see recording below)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/001c5c39-0acf-49ca-8e50-4a6af7d715a0\n\nCan you download the [Godot Android editor](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.godotengine.editor.v4) on your device, and check if mouse capture works there when using the virtual joystick buttons.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689245618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689291158","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2689291158","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2689291158,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gS1OW","user":{"login":"MichaelDawe","id":75983563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTgzNTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75983563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe","html_url":"https://github.com/MichaelDawe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T22:51:49Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T22:51:49Z","body":"> [@MichaelDawe](https://github.com/MichaelDawe) Mouse capture is supported on Android and is being used in the Godot Android editor (see recording below)\n> \n>  Screen_Recording_20250227_142254.mp4 \n> Can you download the [Godot Android editor](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.godotengine.editor.v4) on your device, and check if mouse capture works there when using the virtual joystick buttons.\n\nHello, I have just tried this.  I've found that the mouse does indeed disappear, and reappears at the position I clicked at upon moving it again after releasing the click.  The movement speed increases if I move the mouse further however it's hard to tell if it continues to increase or if it stops when the mouse reaches the edge of the screen.  I tried the MRP opened and played from the android editor and it is still broken.  If you'd like screen recording I can send one.\n\nThanks:)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689291158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689363443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2689363443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2689363443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gTG3z","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T23:47:12Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T17:12:21Z","body":"@MichaelDawe The api works as expected, you just can't call the method from `_ready`.. here's a sample code that works and causes the mouse to be captured on mouse click and release on mouse release:\n\n```gdscript\nextends Sprite2D\n\n\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event is InputEventMouseButton:\n\t\tif event.pressed:\n\t\t\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED)\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_VISIBLE)\n\t\n\tif event is InputEventMouseMotion:\n\t\tposition = event.position\n\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ffbb8887-bac3-4e3d-8134-78d4c57597c2","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689363443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691159495","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2691159495","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2691159495,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gZ9XH","user":{"login":"MichaelDawe","id":75983563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1OTgzNTYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75983563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe","html_url":"https://github.com/MichaelDawe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MichaelDawe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T17:13:05Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T17:13:05Z","body":"Yes this works, thanks :)  \nI also tried `get_tree().create_timer(1.0).timeout.connect(Input.set_mouse_mode.bind(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED))` in the _ready() function.  This hides the mouse however input is no longer received.  It appears that mouse capture has to be called in the _input() function, is there a reason for this and is it likely to be a performance issue?\nThanks :)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691159495/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691187555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2691187555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2691187555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gaENj","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T17:28:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T17:28:06Z","body":"> The api works as expected, you just can't call the method from `_ready`..\n\nIs this documented? It's pretty common to set mouse mode on `_ready` in the main scene when you want e.g. to capture out of the box.\n\nI might have run into this on Chrome OS too a couple of weeks ago and just thought the feature didn't work on Chrome OS: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102657#issuecomment-2650775309\nI'll retest now that I know it doesn't work in `_ready`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691187555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691449772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2691449772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2691449772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gbEOs","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T20:00:50Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T20:00:50Z","body":"> Yes this works, thanks :) I also tried `get_tree().create_timer(1.0).timeout.connect(Input.set_mouse_mode.bind(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED))` in the _ready() function. This hides the mouse however input is no longer received. It appears that mouse capture has to be called in the _input() function, is there a reason for this and is it likely to be a performance issue? Thanks :)\n\n@MichaelDawe This could be a threading issue.. let me do some quick tests to validate.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691449772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2691624893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103196#issuecomment-2691624893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103196","id":2691624893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gbu-9","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","rece